    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's what I implemented for the postcode feature:\n\n**Contract (`openapi.yml`)** \u2014 added an optional `postcode` property to `OwnerFields` with `pattern: '^[0-9]{4}$'`. This makes the generated DTO carry the field and enforces the 4-digit format declaratively, so a malformed postcode (e.g. `\"12\"`) is rejected with 400 via standard Bean Validation. Absent postcode stays valid, keeping the request contract backward-compatible.\n\n**Storage (`Owner.java`)** \u2014 added a `postcode` column with a plain getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it in both directions, so it's stored on create and echoed on read with no mapper changes. Also added the column to `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` and a trailing `NULL` to the positional seed rows in `db/hsqldb/data.sql` (the h2/postgres seeds already use explicit column lists).\n\n**Region validation (new `OwnerPostcodeValidationAdvice.java`)** \u2014 a small, self-contained `@ControllerAdvice`/`Validator` that rejects a 4-digit postcode outside its city's region range (Sydney/NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne/VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane/QLD 4000\u20134099). A city with no known region is left untouched, so any 4-digit postcode is accepted there.\n\n**Structural-impact notes:** I put the cross-field region rule in a brand-new cohesive class rather than growing the existing `OwnerFieldsValidationAdvice.validate` \u2014 its one non-trivial method sits in a class with near-zero surrounding complexity (WMC_other \u2248 0). The only edits to existing methods were trivial getters/setters (CC=1) and declarative config/SQL, keeping every touched function simple.\n\nAll 3 acceptance tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
